From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:39:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebView+WebContent+WebWorker: Launch ImageDecoder
 on demand

Every WebContent and WebWorker process started with an ImageDecoder of
its own, which costs over 20 MiB even for a page or cross-site frame
that has no images, and kept it for its whole life.

Install the image codec plugin without a client, and have it ask the
Browser for a decoder when it first decodes an image. Once the decoder
has had no decodes in flight and no animations for 15 seconds, drop the
client, which makes the decoder exit; the next image starts a new one.
A decoder that crashes is likewise replaced on the next decode, so the
Browser no longer needs to watch for that, nor to send each process a
decoder.

Animation session IDs handed to the page are now the plugin's own,
mapped to the decoder's, since each decoder numbers its sessions from 1
and a session of a decoder that died must not name a new decoder's.

TestImageDecoderIsolation and the ImageDecoder crash report test now
decode an image before looking for a decoder, and the isolation test
checks that a crashed decoder is replaced on the next decode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
